**Authentication successful!** 🎉  

Here’s the response you received from SoundCloud:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **access_token** | `abc123xyz` |
| **expires_in** | `3600` seconds (1 hour) |
| **scope** | `*` (full access) |
| **message** | User authentication successful |

### Next Steps – Adding Playback to Your Website

1. **Store the Access Token**  
   - Save `abc123xyz` securely (e.g., in a server‑side session, encrypted cookie, or backend store).  
   - The token is valid for 1 hour; you’ll need to refresh or re‑authenticate after it expires.

2. **Load the SoundCloud SDK**  
   Add the SoundCloud JavaScript SDK to your page (or use the iframe widget). Example using the SDK:

   ```html
   <!-- Include the SoundCloud SDK -->
   <script src="https://connect.soundcloud.com/sdk/sdk-3.3.2.js"></script>

   <script>
     // Initialize the SDK with your client ID
     SC.initialize({
       client_id: 'client321',
       redirect_uri: 'https://soundcloud.com/callback',
       // optional: you can also pass the access token directly
       // oauth_token: 'abc123xyz'
     });

     // Example: Resolve a track URL and play it
     const trackUrl = 'https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name';

     SC.resolve(trackUrl).then(function(track) {
       // Create a player
       const player = SC.stream(`/tracks/${track.id}`);

       // Play the track
       player.then(function(p) {
         p.play();
       });
     }).catch(function(err) {
       console.error('Error resolving track:', err);
     });
   </script>
   ```

3. **Using the Access Token Directly (optional)**  
   If you prefer to pass the token manually:

   ```js
   SC.initialize({
     client_id: 'client321',
     oauth_token: 'abc123xyz'   // token you just received
   });
   ```

4. **Embedding a Simple Player with an Iframe**  
   If you don’t need the full SDK, you can embed a track or playlist via an iframe:

   ```html
   <iframe width="100%" height="166"
           scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
           src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/TRACK_ID&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true">
   </iframe>
   ```

   Replace `TRACK_ID` with the numeric ID of the track you want to play (you can get it from the `track.id` returned by `SC.resolve`).

5. **Handling Token Expiration**  
   - When the token expires (`expires_in` = 0), redirect the user through the OAuth flow again, or implement a refresh‑token flow if you request offline access.  
   - For a quick re‑auth, just send the user to the authorization URL again:

   ```js
   const authUrl = `https://soundcloud.com/connect?client_id=client321&redirect_uri=${encodeURIComponent('https://soundcloud.com/callback')}&response_type=code&scope=*`;
   window.location.href = authUrl;
   ```

6. **Security Tips**  
   - **HTTPS only**: Your callback URL (`https://soundcloud.com/callback`) must be served over HTTPS.  
   - **State parameter**: Include a random `state` value when you start the OAuth request and verify it on return to protect against CSRF.  
   - **Never expose the client secret** in client‑side code; keep it on the server.

### Quick Checklist

- [ ] Store `abc123xyz` securely (server‑side).  
- [ ] Add the SoundCloud SDK script tag to your page.  
- [ ] Initialize the SDK with `client_id` (and optionally `oauth_token`).  
- [ ] Resolve a track URL or embed an iframe player.  
- [ ] Test playback on a page served over HTTPS.  
- [ ] Implement token‑expiry handling (re‑auth or refresh).  

If you run into any issues (e.g., CORS errors, token problems, or player not loading), let me know the exact error message and I’ll help you troubleshoot!
